  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ndpi_workflow_process_packet",
    "file": "ndpi/example/reader_util.c",
    "description": "Heap OOB read due to missing bounds checks before reading link-layer fields in the DLT_EN10MB path. The function only checks caplen >= eth_offset+28, then unconditionally reads Ethernet header and, when length/type <=1500, reads LLC/SNAP bytes at packet[ip_offset] without verifying that ip_offset + sizeof(ndpi_llc_header_snap) is within header->caplen. With a short/truncated frame this can read 1 byte past the malloc'd packet buffer (ASan shows read at end+0).",
    "conditions": "In fuzz_ndpi_reader, each packet is copied into an exact-size heap buffer of header->caplen and passed to ndpi_workflow_process_packet. A crafted pcap with supported datalink (Ethernet) and caplen around the minimum gate (>=28) but insufficient bytes for the subsequent LLC/SNAP parsing causes out-of-bounds access. Data flow: libpcap parses PoV packet -> harness malloc(caplen)/memcpy -> ndpi_workflow_process_packet DLT_EN10MB branch dereferences beyond packet_checked due to inadequate per-branch length validation."
  },
